  {
    question: 'Do I really need accounting software as a freelancer?',
    answer: 'Yes, even if you have simple finances. Accounting software saves hours during tax season, helps you track deductible expenses you might otherwise miss, provides professional invoices that get you paid faster, and gives you clear visibility into your business finances. The time and tax savings typically exceed the software cost.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What\'s the difference between accounting software and invoicing software?',
    answer: 'Invoicing software focuses solely on creating and sending invoices. Accounting software includes invoicing plus expense tracking, financial reports, bank reconciliation, tax preparation features, and sometimes payroll. Most freelancers benefit from full accounting software since invoicing alone doesn\'t give you the complete financial picture.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can I use free accounting software?',
    answer: 'Yes! Wave offers completely free accounting and invoicing. It\'s excellent for freelancers with straightforward needs. The trade-off is fewer features (no time tracking, limited integrations) and you pay for payment processing. For basic freelance bookkeeping, Wave is genuinely sufficient.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How do I choose between QuickBooks and FreshBooks?',
    answer: 'QuickBooks Self-Employed is better for tax preparation and expense categorization. FreshBooks excels at invoicing, time tracking, and client management. If tax optimization is your priority, choose QuickBooks. If getting paid and managing client projects matters more, choose FreshBooks.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Should I hire an accountant or use software?',
    answer: 'Both! Accounting software handles day-to-day bookkeeping efficiently, while an accountant provides tax strategy and advice. Most freelancers benefit from using software year-round and consulting an accountant quarterly or at tax time. The software makes your accountant\'s job easier (and cheaper).'
  },
  {
    question: 'What accounting software do accountants recommend?',
    answer: 'Most accountants prefer QuickBooks or Xero because they\'re familiar with these platforms. If you work with an accountant, ask their preference before choosing. That said, any reputable software can export data your accountant needs—convenience matters more than brand loyalty.'
  }
];

