  <h2 id="tax-features">Tax Integration Features</h2>

  <h3>Quarterly Tax Estimates</h3>
  <p>
    As a freelancer, you're responsible for quarterly estimated tax payments. The best
    accounting software calculates these automatically:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>QuickBooks Self-Employed:</strong> Automatic quarterly estimates based on your income and deductions
    </li>
    <li><strong>Bonsai:</strong> Tax estimates with Schedule C preview</li>
    <li><strong>FreshBooks:</strong> Reports to help calculate (not automatic estimates)</li>
    <li><strong>Others:</strong> You'll need to calculate manually or use tax software</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Tax Filing Integration</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>QuickBooks + TurboTax:</strong> Direct integration, one-click data transfer</li>
    <li><strong>FreshBooks:</strong> Export reports for your accountant or tax software</li>
    <li><strong>Wave:</strong> Export-ready reports, no direct integration</li>
    <li><strong>Xero:</strong> Many tax software integrations available</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Deduction Tracking</h3>
  <p>
    The software should help you capture every deductible expense. QuickBooks Self-Employed
    excels here with its "swipe to categorize" feature that separates personal and business
    expenses automatically.
  </p>

  <h2 id="mobile-apps">Mobile App Comparison</h2>

  <p>
    A good mobile app is essential for capturing expenses and receipts on the go. Here's
    how they compare:
  </p>

  <h3>Best Mobile Apps</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>QuickBooks Self-Employed:</strong> Excellent receipt scanning, mileage tracking with GPS</li>
    <li><strong>FreshBooks:</strong> Full invoicing and expense tracking on mobile</li>
    <li><strong>HoneyBook:</strong> Client communication and invoicing</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Adequate Mobile Apps</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Wave:</strong> Receipt scanning, basic features</li>
    <li><strong>Xero:</strong> Good but complex</li>
    <li><strong>Bonsai:</strong> Core features available</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Key Mobile Features to Look For</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Receipt capture with OCR (automatic text recognition)</li>
    <li>Quick expense entry</li>
    <li>Invoice creation and sending</li>
    <li>Mileage tracking</li>
    <li>Payment notifications</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="by-freelancer-type">Best Choice by Freelancer Type</h2>

  <h3>Writers and Content Creators</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Recommendation: FreshBooks or Bonsai</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    You need professional invoicing, project tracking, and contracts. Time tracking is
    helpful for hourly work. Tax complexity is usually low, so you don't need QuickBooks'
    tax features.
  </p>

  <h3>Designers and Creatives</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Recommendation: HoneyBook or Bonsai</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Client management matters—questionnaires, mood boards, contracts, and beautiful
    proposals help win work. Pair HoneyBook with Wave for complete accounting.
  </p>

  <h3>Developers and Consultants</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Recommendation: FreshBooks or Xero</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Higher income usually means more tax complexity. You need solid expense tracking and
    professional invoicing. If you're growing toward an agency, Xero scales better.
  </p>

  <h3>Gig Workers and Side Hustlers</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Recommendation: QuickBooks Self-Employed or Wave</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Separating personal and business expenses is critical. QuickBooks handles this elegantly.
    Wave works if you're budget-conscious and organized.
  </p>

  <h3>International Freelancers</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Recommendation: Xero or FreshBooks</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Multi-currency support is essential. Both handle international invoicing well, with
    Xero having the edge for complex multi-currency accounting.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

  <FAQSection faqs={faqData}/>

  <h2>Our Top Recommendations</h2>

  <p>
    After extensive testing, here are our picks:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Best Overall:</strong> QuickBooks Self-Employed — Tax features are unmatched for freelancers</li>
    <li><strong>Best for Invoicing:</strong> FreshBooks — Beautiful invoices that get you paid faster</li>
    <li><strong>Best Free Option:</strong> Wave — Genuinely free with no feature limits</li>
    <li><strong>Best All-in-One:</strong> Bonsai — Contracts, invoices, and accounting together</li>
    <li><strong>Best for Growing:</strong> Xero — Scales from freelancer to agency</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    Most software offers free trials—take advantage of them. Spend a week with your top
    two choices before committing. The right tool pays for itself in time saved and
    deductions captured.
  </p>

